<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description> (255-char cap), and it is INSIDE
        the root element on purpose - a comment ABOVE <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy.

        THE _Count__c SUFFIX IS REQUIRED, NOT STYLISTIC. ARCHITECTURE.md sec 1 rule 4
        reserves the <Subject>_<PastParticiple> shape for BOOLEANS (LOI_Signed__c,
        PSA_Executed__c, SLA_Breached__c). `Fields_Captured__c` IS that shape, so it would
        assert a type this field does not have - rule 9 prohibition 2. The full argument,
        and the two delete-and-recreate repairs this repo has already paid for the same
        mistake (Is_Ready__c, Occupied_Flag__c), are on the Lead twin.

        Numerator of Extraction_Score_Pct__c against the signed-off denominator of NINE
        deal-process keys, which are enumerated once on
        objects/Lead/fields/Extraction_Score_Pct__c. captured + missing = 9, always, on any
        scored row - assert that invariant rather than trusting it.

        CARRIED, NOT RECOMPUTED. Like the percent, it describes the ORIGINAL broker email,
        not the current state of this deal record.

        NULL means not scored (fail-soft); zero captured is a real, scored answer.
    -->
    <fullName>Fields_Captured_Count__c</fullName>
    <description>How many of the nine signed-off deal-process extraction keys were captured from the original broker email, carried from the Lead at conversion. Numerator of Extraction Score %. Null means not scored; zero is a real answer.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <inlineHelpText>Count of deal facts the automated extraction found in the original broker email, out of nine. Pairs with Fields Missing Count.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Fields Captured Count</label>
    <precision>3</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Number</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
